    and escalation chain obliges a party to pay fine and comply by day a due day as its fourth obligation given subject a subject
    and the day > the due day
then escalation chain permits regulatory_body to suspend registration as its fifth obligation given subject the subject
    and it is not the case that escalation chain obliges the party to pay fine and comply by day the due day as its fourth obligation given subject the subject.

% The fifth obligation of escalation chain: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does suspend registration on day a day
    and escalation chain permits the party to suspend registration as its fifth obligation given subject a subject
    and a due day = day + 60
then escalation chain obliges the subject to remedy and apply for reinstatement by day the due day as its sixth obligation
    and it is not the case that escalation chain permits the party to suspend registration as its fifth obligation given subject the subject.

% The sixth obligation of escalation chain: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does remedy and apply for reinstatement on day a day
    and escalation chain obliges the party to remedy and apply for reinstatement by day a due day as its sixth obligation
    and the day <= the due day
then the contract is fulfilled
    and it is not the case that escalation chain obliges the party to remedy and apply for reinstatement by day the due day as its sixth obligation.

when something happens on day a day
    and escalation chain obliges a party to remedy and apply for reinstatement by day a due day as its sixth obligation
    and the day > the due day
then escalation chain obliges regulatory_body to remove from register as its seventh obligation
    and it is not the case that escalation chain obliges the party to remedy and apply for reinstatement by day the due day as its sixth obligation.

% The seventh obligation of escalation chain: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does remove from register on day a day
    and escalation chain obliges the party to remove from register as its seventh obligation
then the contract is breached
    and it is not the case that escalation chain obliges the party to remove from register as its seventh obligation.

